.TH DATAPUMP-GUI 1 "September 2026" "Data Pump 001_00" "User Commands"
.nh
.ad l
.nr HY 0
.ds AD l
.SH NAME
datapump-gui \- graphical audio modem for text and files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B datapump-gui
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B datapump-gui
sends and receives text, exact bit strings and files through an audio interface.
It provides a message editor, file attachments, clipboard actions, QR previews
and live signal plots.
.PP
An ordinary launch opens Fast Modem and listens on the selected audio device.
The Modem menu also offers Robust Modem and Legacy Modem.
Robust uses binary patterns for weak signals; Legacy supports BPSK31,
BPSK125 and Olivia-4/2k text.
The modes have separate settings.
Peers must select matching waveform, source, coding and key settings.
.PP
Robust keeps Baseband Osc, Shift Osc and Margin beside its main Carrier and
Shift frequency controls. Shift 0 disables Shift Osc as N/A and excludes all
Shift-model frequency and phase error. For a positive Shift, the Baseband clock
option shares the selected Baseband model between sampling and mixers, counted
once. Numerical oscillator/search information is under the Link planner's
hideable Model limits and references.
.PP
FLTK and Rev builds provide the same application controls.
The backend is selected at build time and reported by
.BR \-\-version ;
it cannot be switched at runtime.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print a brief usage summary and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and compiled GUI backend, then exit.
.TP
.B \-\-color
Use color where supported; this is the default.
.TP
.B \-\-monochrome
Use grayscale.
The last color or monochrome option wins.
.TP
.B \-\-simulation
Open Robust Modem with a continuous simulated noisy channel instead of live
audio. Transmissions run at computation speed, then replay in the plots.
.SS Robust link settings
Supplying any link setting opens Robust Modem.
These options also accept
.BR \-\-option=value .
Unspecified settings retain their startup defaults.
Link power, path loss and noise describe the planner and simulated channel;
they do not set a radio's RF output power.
.TP
.BI \-\-tx\-dbm " DBM"
Transmit power for the link budget, from \-200 to 100 dBm.
Default: 3.
.TP
.BI \-\-path\-loss\-db " DB"
Path loss, from 0 to 500 dB.
Default: 120.
.TP
.BI \-\-noise\-dbm\-hz " DENSITY"
Receiver noise density, from \-250 to 0 dBm/Hz.
Default: \-164.
.TP
.BI \-\-oscillator " ID"
Baseband oscillator model for bounded receiver search and simulated impairments:
.BR crystal " (default), " gpsdo-xo ,
.BR gpsdo-tcxo " or " gpsdo-ocxo .
.TP
.BI \-\-rf\-oscillator " ID"
Shift oscillator model; the same choices plus ic-7100, default crystal. Inactive at Shift 0.
The IC-7100 RF example does not specify the USB audio clock.
For a legacy positive-Shift shared reference, this flag selects the shared model.
.TP
.BI \-\-reference " independent|shared-radio"
Independent Baseband and Shift references (default), or one shared sampling/mixer
reference for a positive Shift. Shift 0 always uses only the Baseband model.
.B \-\-lf\-reference 0
is a legacy shared-reference shorthand, unrelated to Shift 0. GUI load maps an
active shared model into Baseband Osc and selects Shift Osc's Baseband clock
option. Independent UTC accuracy, region and offset controls do not change that topology.
.TP
.BI \-\-clock\-sync " SPEC"
Default retains the existing epoch search. An explicit example is
GPS_1ms-400ms_region-2564ms_offset: per-station PC accuracy, total propagation
region width centered on the fixed offset. Editable ns/us/ms/s values are accepted.
These are assumptions, not measured audio-device accuracy. Unsupported timing
paths retain the full search and report their limitation.
.TP
.BI \-\-audio\-error " TIME"
Assumed residual audio timing error per station after reported queue compensation;
default 30ms. The editable Audio error dropdown is independent of GPS accuracy,
propagation and oscillator models. Accepts positive ns/us/ms/s durations up to 60s,
subject to the Live search-window limit. This does not change buffering or
establish measured hardware accuracy. Saved parameter lists retain this value.
An unsupported allowance visibly falls back to ordinary playback before private
output; it is not silently enlarged.
.TP
.BI \-\-live\-duplex " yes|no"
Keep hardware capture running during local transmission for physical loopback;
default no. Clear received resets queued input and receiver backlog without
cancelling transmission or clearing its private-key reuse lock.
.TP
.BI \-\-dsss\-factor " 1|10|100|1000"
Additional private outer spreading; 1 is off. Requires a selected key for factors
above one and retains the existing inner private patterns. Experimental receiver
sensitivity and structured-interference qualification are incomplete. Selecting
a factor in the GUI sets Rate 360/36/3.6 Hz for 10x/100x/1000x and stream Carrier
1500 Hz. Explicit command values retain their supplied Rate and Carrier.
.TP
.BI \-\-fhss " off|fake-0.4s-200"
Illustrate 200 channels with 0.4-second dwell in Carrier and Shift displays.
This does not retune hardware or change transmitted audio. Genuine and IC-7100
hardware hopping are unavailable. The illustration is not regulatory certification.
.TP
.BI \-\-search\-margin " N"
Multiply declared frequency and clock accuracy bounds; default 3, minimum 1.
.TP
.BI \-\-target\-snr " DB-HZ"
Set the planner, short-message and long-message target carrier-to-noise-density
ratios, from \-200 to 200 dB-Hz.
This is a planning target, not measured in-band SNR.
.TP
.BI \-\-short\-target\-snr " DB-HZ"
Override the short-message target without changing the planner target.
Default: 32.
.TP
.BI \-\-long\-target\-snr " DB-HZ"
Override the long-message and attachment target without changing the planner
target. Default: 55.
.TP
.BI \-\-rate " FREQUENCY"
Set the nominal rate/bandwidth, from 0.001 Hz to 30 MHz.
Default: 3.6 kHz.
This is not the payload bit rate.
.B \-\-bw
is an alias.
.TP
.BI \-\-carrier " FREQUENCY"
Set the absolute transmitted/received carrier; default 1500 Hz.
Carrier minus Shift must be positive and at most 30 MHz for the real USB stream.
Case-insensitive Hz, kHz, MHz, GHz and THz suffixes, k/m/g/t shorthand, optional
spaces and scientific notation are accepted; a plain number is in Hz.
.B \-\-rf\-carrier
is an alias; matching carrier aliases may be combined.
.TP
.BI \-\-shift " FREQUENCY"
Nonnegative RF translation or LO; default 0 Hz.
Accepts the same frequency units as Carrier.
For Carrier 1.0015 MHz and Shift 1 MHz, the real stream tone is 1500 Hz.
At Shift 0 the same Carrier needs a direct MHz-capable real stream.
.B \-\-rf\-shift
is an alias; choose one shift spelling.
USB is fixed; \-\-sideband upper is a compatibility no-op and lower is rejected.
These settings do not retune hardware or add a complex I/Q interface.
.TP
.BI \-\-dsp\-workspace " PERCENT"
Limit the Robust DSP workspace to 25%, 50% or 75% of available RAM.
Default: 50%.
The percent sign may be omitted.
.TP
.B \-\-auto\-pattern
Select automatic pattern planning, the default.
.TP
.BI \-\-pattern " MODE"
Select
.BR auto-pattern ,
.BR auto-keystream ,
.BR auto-tone ,
.BI pattern- N
with N equal to 3, 4, 6, 8, 12 or 16, or
.BI tone- N
with N equal to 1, 2, 3, 4, 8, 32, 128, 1024, 4096 or 16384.
Tone modes disable private spreading and encryption.
.PP
Frequencies accept Hz, kHz, MHz, GHz or THz case-insensitively, with optional
spaces, scientific notation or k/m/g/t shorthand; bare numbers mean Hz.
Quote a value containing spaces.
The complete combination must fit the local modem and workspace constraints.
.SS Diagnostics
.TP
.B \-\-self\-check
Run shared GUI and transfer checks, then exit.
No display or audio hardware is required.
.TP
.B \-\-smoke\-test
Run the native GUI workflow checks using simulated audio, then exit.
A working graphical display is required.
.TP
.BI \-\-smoke\-dir " DIRECTORY"
Store smoke-test fixtures in DIRECTORY.
By default, use a temporary directory and remove it after success.
.TP
.BI \-\-smoke\-timeout " SECONDS"
Set the smoke workload allowance, from 10 to 1200 seconds.
Default: 100.
.TP
.BI \-\-smoke\-hold " SECONDS"
Keep the window open after successful smoke checks, from 0 to 60 seconds.
Default: 0.
.TP
.BI \-\-smoke\-view " NAME"
Select the initial page and the page shown after successful smoke checks:
.BR console " (default), " planner ,
.BR compression ,
.BR flow ,
.BR transmission " or " fast-modem .
.TP
.BI \-\-smoke\-scroll " FRACTION"
Set the page scroll position after successful smoke checks, from 0 (top) to
1 (bottom). Default: 0.
.SH OPERATION
Choose an audio device and matching peer settings before transmitting.
Use Message for text or Attach file for an attachment; Use text restores the
text draft. Live audio reception pauses during transmission and resumes afterward.
.PP
In Fast Modem, Ctrl+Enter transmits; Enter inserts a newline.
In Robust Modem, Enter transmits by default; the send preference can require
Ctrl+Enter instead.
Cancel stops the current transmission or simulation replay.
.PP
Robust text of 1\(en16 source bytes uses the fixed short dictionary.
Explicit raw-bit input sends precisely its bits, preserving leading zeros and
partial bytes. Neither short path adds a header, padding, FEC or MAC.
Longer text and all attachments use fixed coding intervals.
.PP
Pending Robust receptions expose each newly accepted bit in the same row,
retaining the first 4096 diagnostic bits.
Reception completes only when consecutive fully scored absent symbols cover
at least six seconds. A long symbol must finish before it can count as absent;
cancellation or a decodable prefix does not complete a message.
Pending content cannot be copied or saved as a completed message.
.PP
Completed text can be copied or pasted into the message draft.
Received text and suggested filenames use a restricted ASCII presentation;
disallowed source bytes appear as underscores.
Exact completed attachment bytes remain available for an explicit save.
Received files are never opened or executed automatically.
.PP
Developer mode reveals advanced controls and inspection pages.
The Robust Link planner previews a link independently of the live targets.
Its Launch command can be copied for reuse; Load applies validated settings
without executing a shell command or starting a transmission.
.SH FILES
Keyfiles and attachment paths are chosen through the interface.
Received content is kept in bounded RAM, with no receive cache or temporary
source files on disk. Save needed content before clearing it or closing the
application; older entries may be evicted at the memory limit.
Saving received files and generating keyfiles do not overwrite existing files.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DISPLAY
X display used by Linux desktop builds.
.TP
.B ALSA_PLUGIN_DIR
ALSA plugin directory for Linux live audio.
An explicit value takes precedence over portable-bundle host-plugin discovery.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Normal exit, or successful requested check.
This does not assert that every attempted reception succeeded.
.TP
.B 1
Invalid arguments, startup failure or failed check.
.TP
.B 75
The smoke workload allowance expired with recent sampled-transmission progress.
The diagnostic begins with
.BR "INCOMPLETE GUI_SMOKE_BUDGET:" .
Coverage is incomplete; this is not a successful smoke test.
.SH EXAMPLES
Open the desktop console:
.PP
.nf
    datapump-gui
.fi
.PP
Simulate a Robust link with a common 40 dB-Hz target:
.PP
.nf
    datapump-gui \-\-simulation \-\-target\-snr 40 \-\-rate 1.2kHz
.fi
.PP
Check an installation without opening a window:
.PP
.nf
    datapump-gui \-\-self\-check
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pump (1),
.BR pump-fast (1)
